  "id": "bal",
  "term": "BAL",
  "definition": "BAL, also called dimercaprol, is a chelating agent that has been used in Wilson’s disease, a condition involving excess copper buildup in the liver and brain. The source describes it as clinically toxic, with a narrow safety margin and risks including kidney, cardiovascular, gastrointestinal, and liver-related adverse effects.",
